
export anchor Story_927fc15ab3d25ab1:
    userPrompt:
        \\\
        Adding a story works as it does in Trello and Linear, as spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.creating now says. The Backlog and Next sprint each have an "Add story" line at their foot. Clicking it opens an inline composer at that point: a blank card with its title focused. Enter adds the story to that list and opens another composer beneath it. Escape, or clicking away while the title is empty, discards it. The story is not opened in the side panel. Hovering either list's heading shows a labelled "+ Add" action that adds a story at the top of that list. Ctrl+N adds to the list that has focus, and falls back to Next sprint. This changes the current rule that every new story goes into Next sprint. Accepted proposals still go to the Backlog, and nothing added starts a sprint unless Start automatically would start it when a story is added to Next sprint, as spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.sprint says. Current sprint, Done, and Findings get no composer. Update spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.layout and spec/scope/planning/index.pi#Planning.keyboard to match, then the code.
        \\\

    mode: combined

    model: opus
